00:27.909 --> 00:54.110
And so this morning I will give a brief overview and explanation along with the transmission of the Supplication to the Seven Point Mind Training, Ambrosia of the Mind, the essence of the spiritual tradition coming from the great master Atisha.

01:02.282 --> 01:10.966
I think more than 40 years ago, J. K. Rinpoche gave this teaching in Dordogne, France.

01:12.867 --> 01:16.989
So I was very inspired by this aspiration prayer.

01:17.489 --> 01:24.352
So since then, I try my best to do this every day in my daily prayer.

01:29.883 --> 01:38.509
If we can implement this mind training into our daily life, then I think the essence of all the practice is in this one.

01:45.293 --> 01:48.476
Because during meditation and post meditation,

01:52.508 --> 01:58.613
We are like supposed to be practitioner and we face lots of challenges.

02:01.155 --> 02:19.510
So I think if we cannot implement the teachings we receive and teachings we study when we face our challenges, then I think no matter how many teachings we receive, not so helpful.

02:21.284 --> 02:29.968
So therefore, I think every answer to our problem is very clearly how to deal with this.

02:30.489 --> 02:33.550
It's very clearly mentioned in Lojong practice.

02:33.911 --> 02:40.594
Of course, I think especially nowadays,

02:43.059 --> 02:49.986
It has always been, but nowadays especially, we face a lot of challenges, so people are looking for answers.

02:50.846 --> 02:54.830
And I think many teachers are giving teachings based on Lojong.

02:55.671 --> 03:01.837
So I'm sure most of the things that we will go through today, that you already heard many times.

03:03.618 --> 03:06.561
But we always need a reminder.

03:11.592 --> 03:17.873
So, today we will go through this.

03:17.893 --> 03:35.777
I don't think I have anything new to offer, something new to share with you, but just to remind ourselves.

03:36.057 --> 03:37.797
Last year, I went to Indonesia.

03:40.521 --> 03:43.443
Sumatra Island, where the...

03:55.180 --> 03:56.861
Dharma, selling.

03:57.162 --> 03:58.283
Dharma kirti.

03:59.163 --> 04:01.325
You know, after the COVID, start forgetting.

04:02.226 --> 04:04.607
So whenever I forget, I can blame to the COVID.

04:08.471 --> 04:10.052
So you can implement that.

04:10.172 --> 04:11.333
It works quite well.

04:12.614 --> 04:14.035
Oh, it's COVID, I don't remember.

04:17.832 --> 04:26.955
So they say at one point there were like 11,000 students, almost bigger than, around 11th century, bigger than Nalanda.

04:27.755 --> 04:30.296
So many Buddhists flourished there.

04:31.577 --> 04:34.478
And now there's hardly any, just some ruins.

04:35.038 --> 04:41.660
But anyway, when I went there, I met some professor who did research on this place.

04:42.621 --> 04:44.281
So they told me something very interesting.

04:49.635 --> 04:57.097
In the Indonesian language, when you say, thank you, they say, .

04:58.057 --> 05:09.180
And then this professor told me, the meaning of this is, I give you my happiness and I take your suffering.

05:10.020 --> 05:13.761
And now the Indonesia is kind of a majority Muslim country.

05:14.821 --> 05:17.242
And people don't know, but they still use the word .

05:19.771 --> 05:30.459
Well, it must have been this Lojong master's kind of influence, and still very strong.

05:33.721 --> 05:33.741
.

05:52.841 --> 06:00.305
I begin with the homage.

06:00.565 --> 06:07.529
I bow before the spiritual guides of the supreme vehicle, the source of all that is positive in samsara and nirvana.

06:08.169 --> 06:14.513
May the precious masters grant their blessings so that my mind is purified through the three kinds of faith.

06:16.738 --> 06:23.379
No matter what education we go through, no matter what we may try to learn,

06:45.527 --> 06:49.728
We always need to rely upon somebody to explain it to us, a teacher.

06:50.868 --> 06:59.771
And this is very much the case within the practice, the implementation of the teaching of Buddha, the Dharma.

07:00.451 --> 07:03.952
One must rely upon a fully qualified spiritual teacher.

07:10.023 --> 07:13.726
When I was in the military, I was in the military.

07:13.746 --> 07:14.627
I was in the military.

07:14.647 --> 07:20.151
When I was in the military, I was in the military.

07:20.191 --> 07:24.515
When I was in the military, I was in the military.

07:38.795 --> 07:49.312
When relying on such a spiritual master, it is imperative that one have a sincere appreciation for the individual.

07:50.256 --> 07:53.179
And this isn't to say what they look like.

07:54.421 --> 07:58.285
One likes their form or the way they look or dress and so forth.

07:59.206 --> 08:09.057
Rather, one should look beyond that into the physical, verbal and mental activity of a potential spiritual teacher.

08:09.657 --> 08:20.587
And what one should have a sincere appreciation for is the absence of disturbing emotion and negative mental traits within their very being.

08:20.927 --> 08:22.509
And is that what one should appreciate?

08:30.667 --> 08:35.213
I am very happy to be able to share my story with you today.

08:45.123 --> 09:08.344
For example, when we look around the temple here and we see the images, photographs of myriad spiritual masters, when we look at them, what we should have a sincere appreciation for, or rather what we find ourselves having a sincere appreciation for, is their qualities of experience and spiritual realization.

09:17.124 --> 09:34.540
I tell the people, some of the friends who are connected with me, I always say, your source of inspiration should always, those who are connected with me, I always say, as your source of inspiration.

09:39.635 --> 09:49.723
Then, thanks to now these modern technologies, we have the videos usually recently you viewed, and then we have audio recordings.

09:51.745 --> 09:59.170
Then we have a lot of the teachings transcribed and translated into your own native language.

10:00.271 --> 10:01.853
So we have many, many materials.

10:03.054 --> 10:06.456
So what we need is sort of, wants to sort of inspire.

10:07.637 --> 10:14.961
So I always say, is the main object of your source of inspiration.

10:16.482 --> 10:29.028
And then to give you the transmissions and all those things, then I can do as a kind of, let's say,

10:30.936 --> 10:44.880
Many teachings, they give example of teacher being like doctor, oneself being a patient, and then the teaching like a medicine prescribed by teacher.

10:45.700 --> 10:54.782
I am the pharmacist who just passed down whatever prescription is written there.

10:59.302 --> 11:04.823
So that way, even when I give wang, I always say, think of Chenzi Rinpoche, inseparable from Guru Rinpoche.

11:06.023 --> 11:13.145
And then I just do that, what you call, in between, passing down the lineage.

11:14.345 --> 11:23.487
So therefore, I always, even the wangs, recently in Bhutan, I said, your samaya is connected directly with Chenzi Rinpoche, directly with Chenzi Rinpoche.

11:27.363 --> 11:36.849
So similarly, I think we can still use many of these Masters, even if they are physically not with us, we can always use their teachings.

11:38.330 --> 11:45.334
And looking at their videos, so through them we get inspired by them.

11:47.556 --> 11:48.296
So when we have

11:55.201 --> 12:03.502
I like to say a lot of jokes.

12:04.063 --> 12:11.504
I'm actually more of a stand-up comedian than a teacher.

12:12.245 --> 12:22.667
In the market, when they want to sell some beauty products, then they show you a beautiful male or female photo in the product.

12:24.116 --> 12:31.520
So when you look at that beauty figure, then you say, oh, if I use this product, I may look like he or she.

12:32.601 --> 12:32.941
Isn't it?

12:33.101 --> 12:35.402
So this is also inspiration.

12:36.303 --> 12:37.884
But this is physical inspiration.

12:38.564 --> 12:42.146
So here we are looking at the inner beauty, not the outer beauty.

12:43.447 --> 12:57.618
So when we have these great masters, when we learn, when we study, I think it's very important to read their biographies so that we really get inspired that, oh, it's possible that we can achieve their state of mind.

13:13.716 --> 13:13.756
.

13:13.776 --> 13:13.856
.

13:13.876 --> 13:13.896
.

13:13.916 --> 13:13.936
.

13:13.956 --> 13:13.976
.

13:30.068 --> 13:44.875
So having this appreciation for and inspiration in the particular spiritual teacher with whom one has a particular connection, reflecting again and again upon their teachings,

13:45.855 --> 14:01.727
then there is the conviction arises or the kind of the wish rather arises within us to accomplish a similar spiritual state and through practice then one has the conviction that that is something perfectly possible

14:02.607 --> 14:09.251
And at the same time, we understand that if I only were to tread half of the path, then I wouldn't reach my destination.

14:09.651 --> 14:17.995
So the interest and the desire to complete the training, complete the practice, if you will, arises deeply within one.

14:18.015 --> 14:23.138
And this is the third type of inspiration or kind of trust that is irreversible.

14:27.142 --> 14:38.060
So since we are in the West, culturally, or your culture, not really born in Buddhist environment,

14:39.808 --> 14:52.666
But due to so many different reasons, circumstances, that you all sort of became into this path, the Buddhist path.

14:53.146 --> 14:57.092
So each and everyone has a different reason to join in this path.

14:58.373 --> 15:12.264
due to some kind of emotional problem or sometimes some friend's recommendation or sometimes some of you are sort of inspired, generally inspired by Himalayan kind of culture or Himalayan kind of thing.

15:13.265 --> 15:17.108
So, due to many different reasons that you gather here.

15:19.190 --> 15:31.460
But now, to really become a real good kind of a practitioner or properly join into this path, then we must have a sense of renunciation in the mind.

15:32.260 --> 15:40.707
So that, even though that's not the first case you came here, but we can develop that to become a proper practitioner.

15:41.447 --> 15:43.369
So therefore, renunciation is very important.

15:43.829 --> 15:47.712
So in order to get that, then here are the words, here it says,

15:50.011 --> 15:50.292
Thank you.

15:57.177 --> 16:20.065
May the precious masters grant their blessings so that I may train thoroughly in the preliminaries, recognizing how hard it is to gain the freedoms and advantages and how easily they are lost, so that I strive always to act in accordance with the laws of karma, adopting wholesome deeds and avoiding what is harmful, and develop genuine renunciation for samsara.

16:21.960 --> 16:31.548
So, no matter what the reason you start in the beginning, but now we have to develop this in order to become a sincere practitioner.

16:31.689 --> 16:45.941
We must have the reason for practice is that this common sense of this precious human life, impermanence, law of cause and effect, and then sense of kind of...

16:47.362 --> 16:49.284
Renunciation feeling, raw renunciation.

16:50.505 --> 16:59.475
So therefore, this second verse focuses on the importance of contemplating on those aspects.

17:05.717 --> 17:14.805
So that has to come genuine, has to come genuine, not just knowing how to count the eight this and 18 this, but genuine kind of feeling.

17:16.167 --> 17:22.673
I must have told this story before, but they both live in the hermitage in the forest in Dzogchen Mountains.

17:33.321 --> 17:49.345
And then Pato Rinpoche, when it's time for teaching, he would come out of his cave, and then he would call, Lungto, Lungto, and then Lungto will come somewhere from, I mean, being in Tibet, you've seen the situation, so imagine sorrow comes up.

17:50.725 --> 17:59.868
And then they both sit on the rock, and Pato Rinpoche says, precious human life, precious human life, and then Lungto says, yeah, precious human life.

18:00.268 --> 18:01.108
So they both cry.

18:02.529 --> 18:03.670
And that's one day's teaching.

18:05.872 --> 18:06.953
I heard a story like that.

18:08.214 --> 18:13.458
So it doesn't mean you have to cry, but I think kind of genuine sense of feeling, and that is more important.

18:15.079 --> 18:18.042
So I have teaching went on like that every day, one word, one word.

18:19.483 --> 18:27.290
So just to get kind of deep sense of feeling into this four karhita, four thoughts of, yes, turn your mind.

18:29.909 --> 18:30.810
The second part.

18:52.265 --> 18:54.968
is the main part of the practice, training in bodhicitta.

18:55.808 --> 19:13.343
May the precious Masters grant their blessings so that I may always cultivate the two aspects of bodhicitta, purifying my dualistic perceptions, which have no basis in reality, into all-pervading space, and practicing the profound exchange of my own happiness for others' suffering.

19:19.275 --> 19:19.555
Thank you.

19:34.943 --> 19:40.545
Here then, the first subject in this verse is that of emptiness.

19:42.006 --> 19:54.150
Mention here is made then of a dualistic perception, dualism referring then to the object that is hankered after and the grasping mind that hankers after said object.

19:54.951 --> 20:04.074
Here then, one is advised to purify this dualistic perception, which has no basis in reality, into all-pervading space.

20:06.954 --> 20:07.054
.

20:07.114 --> 20:07.174
.

20:07.194 --> 20:07.214
.

20:07.234 --> 20:07.294
.

20:07.314 --> 20:07.334
.

20:34.585 --> 20:51.340
And so here within the original tradition of the seven-point mind training we find that the emphasis in the main practice or the main part of the practice to training in bodhicitta is the emphasis on, from within the two truths, the ultimate truth.

20:52.381 --> 21:05.669
And so we're encouraged then to reflect upon the empty nature of things as we read, purifying dualistic perception into all pervading space, to think about the empty nature of things.

21:06.390 --> 21:18.257
And with some understanding thereof, one can then genuinely engage in the conventional truth, which is herein the equalizing and exchange of self for other.

21:21.103 --> 21:23.445
This is the story of Tiong Tam Chan-Chu Sam.

21:23.465 --> 21:25.407
He is the father of Tiong Tam Chan-Chu Sam.

21:25.547 --> 21:29.330
He is the father of Tiong Tam Chan-Chu Sam.

21:29.350 --> 21:31.232
He is the father of Tiong Tam Chan-Chu Sam.

21:32.233 --> 21:35.596
He is the father of Tiong Tam Chan-Chu Sam.

21:43.162 --> 21:45.784
In the past, we used to use a laptop to connect to the computer.

21:57.218 --> 22:05.840
And so here we reflect then at the beginning on ultimate bodhicitta, on the empty nature of things.

22:06.000 --> 22:10.801
And with some understanding of that, one can see clearly the plight of others.

22:11.561 --> 22:17.903
And so within the experience of ultimate truth, within the empty nature of things,

22:18.643 --> 22:22.586
one then sees how conventional truth comes to be.

22:23.506 --> 22:30.651
Therein, one sees how others bring about their own experience of dissatisfaction, dukkha, or suffering.

22:31.512 --> 22:43.179
And therein, one engages the practice of giving and taking, reflecting on the equality of all sentient beings, taking their suffering upon oneself, giving one's happiness to them, etc.,

22:44.441 --> 22:51.615
in light of which one aims to give each and every sentient being the same realization of the ultimate truth.

22:57.816 --> 23:13.629
The third part of the aspiration is transforming adversity into the path to awakening.

23:14.449 --> 23:24.538
May the precious Masters grant their blessings so that whatever adversity and suffering may arise, I see them as the wiles of this demon, ego clinging.

23:25.198 --> 23:28.561
and transform them into the path towards awakening.

23:54.905 --> 24:02.890
As it is said, we are individuals who are within the confines of the three realms of samsara.

24:03.871 --> 24:12.116
And if we were to wonder how this came about, initially there is an idea, a conception of an autonomous or independent self.

24:13.137 --> 24:22.743
And then there is an addiction towards that, a grasping at it, and based thereupon action, and based thereupon a result, and there through dissatisfaction and suffering.

24:27.072 --> 24:35.434
So I think it is worthwhile to put some thinking on this kind of I-thing.

24:36.494 --> 24:41.895
I am sure we hear almost every teaching, you talk about this ego clinging and all that.

24:44.576 --> 24:54.918
So when we are born, there is no name, and then we get the name,

24:56.747 --> 25:02.895
then we somehow cling to that name, notion, of all so-and-so is calling me.

25:04.937 --> 25:15.070
And then, slowly, that sort of becomes a bigger and bigger kind of influence into our daily life.

25:21.325 --> 25:32.774
So when I was in Portugal, some of non-Buddhist friends, I actually tried to go to the gym a little bit.

25:33.414 --> 25:36.957
So non-Buddhist friends, they asked me, what's your name?

25:37.717 --> 25:42.101
So the closest name for Ram Jam I could find in Portuguese is Roberto.

25:50.045 --> 25:51.367
He says, oh, I'm Roberto.

25:53.189 --> 25:59.136
And then one day I was doing exercise and I forgot my name was Roberto.

26:02.480 --> 26:04.282
And somebody was calling Roberto, Roberto.

26:04.302 --> 26:05.283
I said, who is this calling?

26:07.125 --> 26:09.128
I cannot associate myself with my name.

26:19.731 --> 26:26.015
So we usually talk about my clothes.

26:27.716 --> 26:29.057
Once there is me, my clothes.

26:30.158 --> 26:33.380
Then my body, my hand.

26:35.142 --> 26:37.363
So we are the owner of this, right?

26:39.265 --> 26:41.126
So if you think a little bit,

26:42.618 --> 26:43.840
Who is this mind?

26:44.241 --> 26:46.023
Normally people will say, oh, it's the mind.

26:48.026 --> 26:50.569
But when it comes to mind, we always say, my mind.

26:51.450 --> 26:52.812
We don't say the I mind.

26:55.235 --> 26:58.240
So, I think we are not really clear about who is me.

27:00.594 --> 27:05.080
So this doesn't need a very deep kind of philosophical studies.

27:05.361 --> 27:06.422
It's just simple thinking.

27:07.443 --> 27:08.985
When you say, my mind.

27:09.106 --> 27:14.413
So outside of mind, there's supposed to be another who owns your mind.

27:16.102 --> 27:33.628
So this kind of analytical thinking is very, very helpful, I think, and I think very important because we consider this I so precious, this so-called I.

27:39.109 --> 27:47.016
So when we so much focus on I, I, I, then everything becomes very big.

27:49.679 --> 28:01.430
Quite often in the teachings it says that if you put a handful of salt in a glass of water, then it becomes not drinkable because it becomes very salty.

28:02.967 --> 28:16.096
So because there is a very small mind focusing on the eye, a similar handful of salt you put in a big bucket of water, then you don't taste the salt so much.

28:17.157 --> 28:32.027
So similarly, instead of just focusing on the eye, this eye, if we can open up our mind a little bit, then all these small problems, all the problems we think are very big, become very small.

28:34.662 --> 28:40.707
So that is, I think, a very good antidote for whenever we face a problem in our life.

28:42.368 --> 28:45.250
If you always sort of search, what is this problem?

28:45.991 --> 28:47.252
What is the cause of this problem?

28:47.292 --> 28:49.994
It always becomes focused to this I.

28:58.945 --> 29:23.995
Some story I used to tell that if you are walking by a shop and there is a beautiful expensive vase in the showroom glass and you walk by and then someone is cleaning the glass and then push the vase and breaks.

29:25.759 --> 29:29.262
So we'll say, oh, such a pity, that beautiful vase is broken.

29:30.803 --> 29:35.286
Now similar, same scenario, now that vase belongs to you.

29:36.847 --> 29:40.730
So now once it belongs to you, then we order the label saying, this is mine.

29:42.491 --> 29:45.593
Then somebody breaks it, then becomes catastrophe.

29:47.365 --> 29:47.706
Isn't it?

29:47.786 --> 29:52.252
So I think many problems in our life are because of this.

29:52.612 --> 29:56.277
We put this sticker of me, me, me everywhere.

30:01.115 --> 30:06.962
I think it is worthwhile to do some analytical thinking whenever we face some problems.

30:09.665 --> 30:18.296
I think one very important thing is, when we face these small, small problems in our daily life, then I think we should

30:19.377 --> 30:25.579
quickly try to implement the teachings, thinking, oh, this is a small problem, just let go.

30:26.159 --> 30:33.662
And then when the big, big sort of circumstances hit us, then we are not ready to challenge or face that.

30:34.522 --> 30:44.865
So small problems, small thing, when it hurts us, then I think we have to work on that.

30:46.986 --> 30:47.366
Example,

30:49.163 --> 30:55.349
When you drive in Europe, I used to drive in Asia, where there's not much rules.

30:55.489 --> 30:57.031
You can more or less do whatever you want.

30:58.312 --> 31:00.574
If you have a bigger car, you can just more or less go.

31:01.314 --> 31:02.836
Just push the small cars away.

31:04.017 --> 31:09.102
But in the West, there are so many rules that in the beginning when I drop, I get so much honk.

31:09.302 --> 31:09.542
Bang!

31:10.163 --> 31:10.843
Bang!

31:11.724 --> 31:14.647
So every time, honk is not a very pleasant feeling.

31:15.287 --> 31:18.070
Because actually they are shouting at you, isn't it?

31:19.031 --> 31:27.257
So even these situations, when you feel a little bit unpleasant feeling, then I think we have to start working on that.

31:28.518 --> 31:36.005
So small, small kind of unpleasant feeling, we have to recognize, okay, this is due to our ego clinging.

31:37.746 --> 31:43.670
And then we get used to kind of dealing with problems.

31:44.911 --> 31:46.872
Right away, we implement that.

31:48.393 --> 31:51.075
So the teachings, teachers like George Kensington used to say,

31:55.035 --> 32:02.924
when the circumstances arise, then that's where you judge whether you are a practitioner or not.

32:04.185 --> 32:11.834
So when everything is fine, when everything is going well, of course we can think, oh, I'm doing good practice.

32:14.672 --> 32:24.975
But when circumstances arise, then if we cannot handle it, then our practice and our kind of life is going different direction.

32:26.056 --> 32:33.858
So whenever some small circumstance arise, we try to implement right away the teachings, especially like the Lojong teachings.

32:36.005 --> 32:38.286
Then we get kind of used to that thing.

32:39.106 --> 32:45.009
And then when sometimes face bigger challenges, we are ready to face those challenges.

32:45.269 --> 32:58.135
And I think if you're a good lojong practitioner, not only sort of able to face those challenges, but you sort of look forward for challenges, isn't it?

32:58.335 --> 33:02.737
Oh, now let me see whether I can handle this kind of harsh world.

33:04.432 --> 33:04.752
or not.

33:05.553 --> 33:06.993
So sort of look forward.

33:08.434 --> 33:15.077
There is no kind of fear that I might face some difficulty and challenge because what you have been trained for that.

33:17.878 --> 33:18.179
Okay?

33:20.220 --> 33:20.240
.

33:32.780 --> 33:34.741
applying the practice throughout one's life.

33:35.721 --> 33:52.267
May the precious masters grant their blessings so that I may focus upon the essence of the practice throughout my life and always apply the five strengths of pure thought and pure deed, gathering merit, purifying obscurations, and making prayers of aspiration.

33:58.105 --> 34:03.550
In the end, I was able to receive a message from the Lord.

34:03.570 --> 34:06.292
I was able to receive a message from the Lord.

34:06.352 --> 34:09.895
I was able to receive a message from the Lord.

34:09.915 --> 34:11.096
I was able to receive a message.

34:13.372 --> 34:19.016
So the practice of mind training should be one that we carry throughout our entire life.

34:19.836 --> 34:27.161
It is not an instruction that we put into practice for a short time and then give up on it thinking that there is something else to do.

34:27.821 --> 34:35.506
Rather, the practice should be completely integrated with our very being and carried throughout the entirety of our lives.

34:37.908 --> 34:37.968
.

34:37.988 --> 34:38.008
.

34:38.068 --> 34:38.128
.

34:38.188 --> 34:38.208
.

34:38.228 --> 34:38.248
.

34:51.511 --> 35:12.234
And it's important that when we make the accumulations of merit, for example, if we go to a temple and we make an offering, perhaps a butter lamp or something, or if we are circumambulating temples, stupas and what have you, it's imperative that when making merit, we always dedicate that merit to the development of bodhicitta within ourselves.

35:13.316 --> 35:13.336
.

35:13.356 --> 35:13.436
.

35:13.476 --> 35:13.516
.

35:13.536 --> 35:13.576
.

35:13.596 --> 35:13.616
.

35:34.413 --> 35:41.738
And within the mind-training tradition there is the resolution of practice.

35:42.338 --> 35:44.019
So we talk of the kind of five

35:47.527 --> 35:49.108
the powers of the practice.

35:49.148 --> 35:56.915
One of them is of the resolution to actually engage or to thoroughly familiarize oneself with the instructions.

35:56.975 --> 36:09.647
So for example, we may take a week, we make sure that we are very mindful in absorbing the teachings within our very being during that time span and thereafter we can perhaps extend it to two weeks and so forth.

36:16.848 --> 36:25.635
The measure of mind training is given thus.

36:26.596 --> 36:40.127
May the precious Masters grant their blessings so that with joyful self-assurance and freedom of mind I may bring all adverse circumstances onto the path and everything may become a remedy to ego clinging.

36:42.389 --> 36:42.409
.

36:42.449 --> 36:42.509
.

36:42.590 --> 36:42.610
.

36:42.630 --> 36:42.670
.

36:42.690 --> 36:42.710
.

36:55.832 --> 37:01.576
And so essentially the measure of mind training is how familiar you are with the practice.

37:02.316 --> 37:13.984
And so when you meet with certain circumstances then the mind training teaching should kick in and then assist you with whatever difficulties or circumstances you are facing.

37:24.294 --> 37:24.975
Thank you.

37:37.283 --> 37:46.969
So I'm a little bit, my mind's gone a little bit blank at the moment, so I can doubly blame COVID and also the flu that I'm suffering from at the moment.

37:47.829 --> 37:53.432
Sometimes we say like, I think it's sort of become habit in Tibetan tradition, like .

37:53.452 --> 37:56.554
So whatever circumstances happens, this kind of .

38:09.743 --> 38:11.605
If you sort of fall, there is a lama chain.

38:12.706 --> 38:15.229
So likewise, I think it has to be a kind of habit.

38:19.973 --> 38:20.774
I tell you a joke.

38:24.277 --> 38:43.902
An occidental Buddhist was flying in the plane and then the plane hit the turbulence and the plane was shaking very badly and he was praying to Guru Rinpoche.

38:43.942 --> 38:50.824
He was praying very hard to Guru Rinpoche and then finally the plane landed safely and he said, oh thank God.

39:07.626 --> 39:21.618
And so no matter what circumstances, negative we face, rather the thing that we should thank is the mind training teaching.

39:22.059 --> 39:24.041
Thank instead of God, the mind training.

39:24.901 --> 39:30.923
So, the Lama said, if you want to go to the forest, you have to go to the forest.

39:30.943 --> 39:35.364
If you want to go to the forest, you have to go to the forest.

39:55.168 --> 40:03.093
As it is said in the mind training tradition, our practice of mind training should be as agile as a good horse rider.

40:04.113 --> 40:10.157
So if you're very good at riding horses, you're very skilled in that endeavor,

40:10.717 --> 40:16.682
Then when you're galloping along a plain or walking gently through a forest, everything is fine.

40:16.722 --> 40:20.265
And then all of a sudden you come upon rough ground, etc.

40:20.325 --> 40:21.266
It makes no difference.

40:21.866 --> 40:28.052
The horse rider is able to ride the horse according to the ground within which he finds himself.

40:28.852 --> 40:37.679
So accordingly, with mind-training teaching, no matter what circumstances we may run into, we should, like a good horse rider, be able to navigate it.

40:41.743 --> 40:49.889
The sixth point then are the commitments of mind training.

40:50.049 --> 41:03.980
Again we read, May the precious masters grant their blessings so that I may keep my promises without hypocrisy and always remain impartial and free of ostentation, guarding the lojung commitments as I do my very life.

41:05.424 --> 41:05.785
Thank you.

41:13.742 --> 41:25.748
So accordingly, as I mentioned before, if we are able to utilize the lojong or the mind training instructions to face small challenges, when the big challenges of life come along, we are prepared.

41:36.855 --> 41:52.021
Accordingly, if we kind of ignore the small challenges of life and perhaps don't apply the mind training instructions there, when the larger challenges of life come along, when circumstances in life change, then we won't be able to deal with them.

41:52.141 --> 41:54.201
It will be a huge difficulty.

42:04.085 --> 42:13.496
So the essence of the commitment is not just to deal with small problems and leave the big ones, rather we should deal with all problems regardless of their size.

42:24.841 --> 42:39.908
Someone I know did some wrongdoings, or maybe he did not really commit a crime, but somehow he was put in a kind of bad situation in prison.

42:41.429 --> 42:45.733
And then he received many teachings, person has received many teachings.

42:46.774 --> 42:57.766
But then he came out after a while and he was so angry at the people who mistreated him, or prison guard or whatever.

42:58.747 --> 42:59.508
He was so angry.

43:00.154 --> 43:06.023
Then I said, yeah, but what about the teachings you receive, the mind training teachings you receive?

43:06.564 --> 43:08.366
What about generating love and compassion?

43:09.247 --> 43:12.412
He said, their behavior is beyond loving compassion.

43:16.950 --> 43:24.154
There is another lady I know from a very noble family.

43:26.936 --> 43:30.478
She works in her father's company, a very rich family.

43:31.819 --> 43:39.783
Because her father made her sign some documents, the father ran away and she was put in prison.

43:41.004 --> 43:48.731
from living like a princess life to a prison with six other ladies, all very wild ladies.

43:50.432 --> 43:53.275
And then I used to send her some books.

43:53.595 --> 43:57.358
She received actually Mahayana teaching and also she had practiced Vajrayana teaching.

43:58.019 --> 43:59.060
And she handled very well.

44:00.161 --> 44:03.363
And she said she was in the jail, she was reading them.

44:05.465 --> 44:13.008
the mind training, it was really helpful that she managed to go through her time.

44:13.228 --> 44:16.170
Because it's not her mistake, it was her father's mistake.

44:16.630 --> 44:21.552
And then she got, because she signed some documents, she was in prison for a few years.

44:22.452 --> 44:27.695
But we could see how she can actually implement the teachings that she received.

44:28.596 --> 44:35.220
So that's how I think we have to handle, we have to implement the teachings.

44:37.081 --> 44:50.809
Also, I heard some time ago that Burmese, everybody knows Burmese Aung San Suu Kyi, she was also raising the enlightened courage when she was in house arrest, and they said, really, help her.

44:52.150 --> 45:04.205
So like that, I think sometimes we have people who you can really see that how much these teachings can benefit their difficult situations.

45:04.545 --> 45:06.948
So that's what the teaching is all about.

45:08.467 --> 45:18.317
So we have received the highest teachings, most profound teachings, then we have difficulty in life, then we are not able to handle and then panic.

45:19.238 --> 45:21.461
Then the teaching is not really helping you.

45:27.778 --> 45:57.325
And I think it's also very important to, especially in the kind of place where there's non-Buddhist people, I think we have to remain very low profile, not showing off, saying, oh, I'm Buddhist and this and that, but outwardly very kind of common, but inwardly big difference, big heart.

46:01.127 --> 46:09.451
I think also we have a responsible, being a Buddhist, responsible to inspire others, right?

46:09.551 --> 46:10.271
Inspire others.

46:10.552 --> 46:16.655
Like sometimes in a family, some of you, maybe not all of them are Buddhists.

46:17.535 --> 46:29.598
When you become Buddhist, if they can see that you've become a better person, you're becoming a more open-minded person, then it will inspire your other family who are not so much into Dharma.

46:30.678 --> 46:37.100
And you become Buddhist and you become crazy, then it's not going to inspire.

46:40.600 --> 46:44.461
We do have quite a number of crazy people, isn't it, in the covenant?

46:48.162 --> 47:00.207
I have a friend who said, before he became Buddhist, he was quite wild, and then he became Buddhist, and then he realized how wild he was before he became Buddhist, how crazy he was.

47:01.848 --> 47:08.090
And then after some time he spent with the Buddhist community, he said, oh, now I realize how crazy the Buddhists are.

47:10.342 --> 47:15.026
And then I said, at the end you will realize how everything is crazy, then you have achieved.

47:17.567 --> 47:24.172
So I think very important to live very low profile, very normal kind of life, unless you are monastric, it's different.

47:24.813 --> 47:29.556
But normal dress, normal, just being very normal, and then be a good person.

47:29.957 --> 47:37.602
And that will encourage our family, friends, saying, oh, this really, I met many people who said that it changed.

47:38.743 --> 47:45.265
Recently, I visited one school in America.

47:46.765 --> 47:49.566
They have a program in the public school.

47:50.786 --> 47:53.967
They don't call it Buddhism, but they call it something like compassion.

47:55.087 --> 47:59.568
And all the public schools, they do some activity related to the compassion.

48:00.288 --> 48:01.488
They're doing some experiment.

48:03.489 --> 48:05.069
Then the teacher is also not Buddhist.

48:05.269 --> 48:07.070
It was an African-American lady.

48:08.971 --> 48:23.943
And they said it helped all the children's behavior using that some technique, karma binding, and little meditation, and then teaching them how to care for others without using the very difficult dharma word.

48:24.844 --> 48:26.705
So they do twice a week, they do training.

48:27.967 --> 48:30.048
And then I asked the teacher, how was it doing?

48:30.068 --> 48:31.289
She said, oh, it's really good.

48:31.449 --> 48:34.672
She said like how the African-American talk.

48:34.772 --> 48:35.573
It's really good.

48:36.685 --> 48:41.971
Not only the kids, but even when the parents, they fight, the kids will come to parents.

48:42.291 --> 48:56.907
So the chain reaction you see from that school, it's in Louisville in America, that they're really seriously thinking how to implement some kind of the Buddhist technique into main education system.

48:58.067 --> 49:01.229
And they have a, they call it control school.

49:01.429 --> 49:04.871
One school, they have twice a week meditation, and one school don't have.

49:05.631 --> 49:17.177
So if they can prove that that school with the meditation can be better than the other school, then they were seriously thinking how to implement this technique method into the American education system.

49:18.238 --> 49:20.459
Because there's a lot of violence going on in America.

49:21.980 --> 49:37.008
So like that, how can the children, little bit of, not very deep Buddhist philosophy teaching, just basic teaching how to be good, how to be caring for others, already they are able to change their parents.

49:37.588 --> 49:43.351
Parents like, because public school, most of the children are from little bit poor background family.

49:44.372 --> 49:47.354
So then there's some lot of violent and things.

49:47.414 --> 49:49.755
So the children's able to change their parents.

49:50.835 --> 49:53.436
So that was very encouraging to see that.

49:54.057 --> 50:07.542
So similarly, we call ourselves Buddhists, and I think we have to, even without talking, just being a good human being, being a good person, will encourage others into the path.

