53:16.936 --> 53:19.537
It's wonderful to repeat this at the beginning.

53:20.197 --> 53:26.880
And it doesn't matter what language you use, whether it be in English or whatever language, it makes really no difference.

53:27.321 --> 53:32.503
Because the point of repeating something every day is to bring the meaning to mind.

53:36.547 --> 53:40.280
I think last year, you saw this Dalai Lama visit our Nyingma Mela in Bodh Gaya.

53:40.300 --> 53:40.862
Was it last year?

53:42.312 --> 53:44.534
No, this year.

53:44.814 --> 53:47.375
This year, beginning of His Holiness' visit.

53:47.956 --> 54:08.768
And his advice to that time, he said that, from morning when we get up, then we should make the aspiration prayer that the whole day, this day, whatever we do, we will try to engage with dharma.

54:09.428 --> 54:16.454
So this I found very, very important because we always think that, oh, sometime later I'm going to do something.

54:17.715 --> 54:18.856
We sort of forget today.

54:19.897 --> 54:32.447
So His Holiness' advice was like, when you get up in the morning, then we make a kind of commitment with Thamjad, that whole day, this today, the whole day, I will howl, I will ...

54:33.347 --> 54:37.330
and bring my whole day into the practice of dharma.

54:37.731 --> 54:43.475
So that was his advice during his visit at the beginning of this year in Nyingmabal.

54:43.515 --> 54:49.900
He very kindly visited and stayed maybe one or two hours.

54:50.120 --> 54:51.921
So I think today we are on time.

